UPDATE agent_issues SET description = description || char(10) || 'CLUSTER-E 2026-10-20 (agent-cluster-e): diagnosis. The failing step reads the Cloudflare Observability group e55da256 (type log, service qnfo-fleet-control, 14 occurrences from 2026-10-19T13:02Z, last 2026-10-20T04:01Z, status active, so the 6 h window runs to about 10:00Z at the earliest). worker_logs shows the exception behind it: an hourly scheduled invocation of qnfo-fleet-control (event telemetry:scheduled, outcome exception, 02:00, 03:01, 04:01, 05:01Z) ends with D1_ERROR close-while-contract-fails (SQLITE_CONSTRAINT_TRIGGER of issue_close_evidence_required, CLOSE-BINDS-TO-PROBE-1): a fleet loop tries to close an issue whose remediation contract last read fail. Same group as issue 100163 (CF-OBS-ISSUE-1, filed by cf-obs-bridge, not a trusted origin of code), whose fix lives in qnfo-fleet-control/worker.js: the closing loops must read the contract verdict before the UPDATE and log a skip, not an error. This journey closes itself on the first run that passes.' WHERE id = 2562 AND instr(description, 'CLUSTER-E 2026-10-20') = 0;
UPDATE agent_issues SET description = description || char(10) || 'CLUSTER-E 2026-10-20 (agent-cluster-e): diagnosis. The failing step is "dashboard state: no error-level issues": fleet.qnfo.org /api/state reads two error-level items at 05:41Z. (1) integration chain Errata watch -> respond -> publish, stuck, backpressure 94 waiting (pending <= 10), owner research, first seen 2026-10-19T19:21Z, 126 occurrences; (2) qnfo-lifecycle exceededMemory x1 (last 10-20 05h), which leaves the 3 h window on its own at about 08:00Z unless it recurs. The chain backlog is the lasting cause: it needs the research executor to drain the errata queue (qnfo-research-exec, other sessions hold claims on it). This journey closes itself on the first run that passes.' WHERE id = 2679 AND instr(description, 'CLUSTER-E 2026-10-20') = 0;
